# copyover (act_wiz.c do_copyover), up to the exec: both drivers stub it (the C's wraps execl), print what it would
# run, and fail as a failed exec does, so do_copyover then says "Copyover FAILED!". The recovery after a real exec
# (copyover_recover) is checked by sim smoke's copyover steps, in WSL (#91, decision 3).
# - Seraph (56) can't copyover (it's level 60); Smokegod (60) does
# - Delver, playing, and Pupil, writing a note (IS_IN_GAME counts that as playing), are saved and told to remain
#   seated; Rambler, still at the password prompt, is told the game is
#   rebooting and dropped; copyover.data lists who was saved, by descriptor, name and host, and ends with -1
@connect god
Smokegod
smoke123
@return
@return
@connect ser
Seraph
smoke123
@return
@return
@connect d
Delver
psswrd
@return
@connect p
Pupil
psswrd
@return
note write
@connect r
Rambler
@as ser
copyover
@as god
copyover
@file copyover.data
@file ../player/Delver
